;; M4N slice 3 regression (the slice-1/2 admission hole): a cone holding
;; BOTH an edited negated input (~b) and a derived negated relation (~m,
;; fed by a2).  A flush editing b and a2 together must NOT take the
;; edit-staging arms (m's maintained transitions would go unstaged) nor
;; the pure-derived arm (b's edit journal is not a maintained journal in
;; the reader schedule) -- it falls back to rerun.  A b-only flush keeps
;; m outside the cone and stays precise.

table (a int)
table (a2 int)
table (b int)
table (m int)
table (h int)

rule
(a2 X)
-->
(m X)

rule
(a X)
~(b X)
~(m X)
-->
(h X)
